WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:07.460
<i>Can't you see that you are sweet?</i>

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:15.050
<i>Oh, let me love you so.</i>

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:24.460
War in the Pocket

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:31.150
<i>As I look up, the sky above seems so far away...</i>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:31.150
<i>miageru sora wa tooi kedo</i>

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.320
<i>...but there are dreams that even it can't hold.</i>

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.320
<i>kakae kirenai yume ga aru</i>

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:48.290
<i>Oh, yes, I want to slip away from this artificial world...</i>

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:48.290
<i>sou yo, tsukurareta sekai no naka wo mukidashite</i>

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:52.670
<i>...and make myself free.</i>

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:52.670
<i>jiyuu ni naritai</i>

00:00:52.750 --> 00:01:06.890
<i>I can keep on running till I finally reach the sky.</i>

00:00:52.750 --> 00:01:06.890
<i>hashi ni tsuzukete sora ni todoteba</i>

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:17.280
<i>Since I can believe that I can become the wind someday...</i>

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:17.280
<i>kaze ni nareru to sou shinjiteru kara</i>

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:23.450
<i>I never give up forever.</i>

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:06.930
Say It Ain't So, Bernie!

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:10.320
<i>Report begins.</i>
<i>Operation Rubicon has failed.</i>

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.620
<i>Gundam still in Side 6.</i>

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.450
<i>Status of Cyclops team:</i> <i>Unknown. Report ends.</i>

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:26.960
No! I said stop! Get away from here!

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:29.470
But the commander ordered it.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:31.840
Killing! What's the meaning of this?!

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:33.720
What do you mean, sir?

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:37.140
I never gave you permission to use nuclear warheads!

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.640
I never asked for it, sir.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:42.440
Dammit, are you planning to break the treaty?!

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.320
Side 6 never ratified the Antarctic Treaty.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:47.690
That isn't the point!

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:52.280
Furthermore, my actions are outside of your jurisdiction.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:54.370
I am this base's commander and...

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:56.990
Sir!

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:11.050
Continue the loading! As of now, I am in command of Granada!

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:12.800
The police?

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:15.850
They said they wanted to ask you directly.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:17.180
Where are they?

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:21.770
Next to that Zeon mobile suit. They insisted on meeting you there.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:49.210
So, a cute girl like you is the pilot of that mobile suit, huh?

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:50.800
At your service, sir.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:53.170
You're the one who got this thing?

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:53.840
Yes, sir.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:59.600
Two surviving Zeon soldiers apparently fled into the suburbs.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.730
Can you recall anything that might help us?

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:04.190
No, nothing particular.

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.810
Anything might be helpful.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.020
I'm sorry, sir.

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:13.530
Well, then, we have information suggesting there was...

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:17.660
...inside help on this attack. What do you think of that?

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.330
I'm not sure what you mean, sir.

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:21.410
This is getting us nowhere.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:23.080
Is that all, sir?

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:26.290
No, it isn't! If they move again, more innocent people may die!

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:30.040
Strange, don't you think?

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:32.670
How the Zeon began attacking...

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:36.090
...a supposedly neutral colony so openly?

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:38.340
Now, why do you suppose that is?

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:39.720
No comment, sir.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:43.890
I see. You know the answer, but just won't say it.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.730
The Federal Forces have been secretly developing mobile suits...

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:51.730
...in a neutral colony while saying they're just stationing themselves here.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:55.150
That's why the Zeon came! Isn't that right?

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:56.530
No comment, sir.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:01.160
246 people dead!
572 people wounded!

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.620
That's the number of victims from yesterday.

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:07.290
I don't want that many people getting hurt again.

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:11.540
If we didn't fight, more people would have been killed!

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:13.050
It couldn't be helped.

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:15.970
I know what you're trying to say...

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:20.430
...but nobody should ever have to die because "it couldn't be helped."

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:22.760
The number of victims isn't the point.

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:40.740
- This is horrible!
- My God!

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:43.620
I heard some surviving Zeeks got into the city.

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:45.450
If I find them, they're dead!

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:49.330
They didn't have to fight in the colony...

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:50.880
What were the Feds thinking?!

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:52.790
- It's a kid!
- Oh, the poor thing!

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:33.580
Bernie, is it? The Gundam... Is it?

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:38.760
It's...

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:42.180
Misha destroyed it.

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:44.260
Come on, let's get out of here.

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:49.850
Bernie... You're a terrible liar.

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:52.810
Captain? Captain!

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:56.520
Captain...

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:07.370
Hardy is... Steiner is dead?

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:10.500
What about Misha?

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:11.870
Dead.

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:14.000
And the young fellow with the black hair?

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:14.880
Dead.

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:16.130
I see...

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:21.420
You have to use that passport and escape! Immediately!

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:23.930
I thought I'd wait for the heat to die down.

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:26.430
No! You have to leave now!

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:28.510
I think it'd be safer to wait a little.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.520
I know, but...

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.350
But what?

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:37.480
All right, listen carefully.

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:40.690
If the Gundam isn't destroyed by Christmas night...

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:42.950
...a fleet will come from Granada.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:46.570
They're going to destroy this colony with a nuclear missile.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.910
They... They wouldn't!

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:50.830
God help us, they would.

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:56.500
You have to get out of here, boy. Run away and live!

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:58.460
Aren't you going to leave, too?

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:07.970
I'm an old man... And I like this colony.

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:23.030
Bernie, it's me. Bernie.

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:31.740
You were careful to watch your back?

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:34.710
Are the police looking for me?

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:36.790
I see.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.750
Sit down. Let's eat.

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:44.800
What's wrong?

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:54.730
People die really easily, don't they?

00:08:54.770 --> 00:08:57.350
Are you saying that again?! Stop thinking about it!

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:58.480
But!

00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:01.070
People die because they just get unlucky!

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:04.280
You can be a captain or a nobody. When your luck runs out, you die!

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:07.070
That's how war is! Understand?

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:11.990
Christ...

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:14.290
Here, eat already.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:23.050
Al... I'm leaving this colony today.

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:28.010
- You're running away?
- Yes.

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:30.930
Why?! But that...

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:33.720
What about that Feddie mobile suit?!

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:35.180
You're just giving up?!

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:38.850
I know how you feel, but sometimes it's better to run than...

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:42.480
We can still do it! What about everyone who died?!

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:44.400
Listen to me!

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:48.990
In three days, if the Gundam isn't destroyed by Christmas night...

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:50.780
...a fleet will come from Granada.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:54.540
They're going to destroy the colony with a nuke.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:56.370
Then...

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:00.880
This colony's going to be destroyed! There's no one who can stop it!

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:04.420
You have to leave, Al. Can't you and your mom go on a trip or something?

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:08.300
But all we have to do is destroy it by Christmas, right?

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:10.090
I can't do that!

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:12.140
You can do it, Bernie!

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:15.600
No, I can't! How do I beat that monster?!

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:19.730
Yeah, it's new, but it's just a little faster. If we fix the Zaku...

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:22.310
If we fix it, then what? Are you going to pilot it?

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:27.900
Al, the truth is I've never even shot down <i>one</i> mobile suit!

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:31.820
You said you only needed one more kill to be an ace!

00:10:31.910 --> 00:10:33.030
I didn't!

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:33.910
Did so!

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:40.040
I'm a rookie, Al. A fifth wheel. Just over here for the ride!

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:44.540
That's a lie! You're just lying 'cuz you're scared!

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:48.090
Damn right I'm scared! I'd be crazy not to be.

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:50.340
Go on, call me a coward or whatever you want.

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:51.510
Wait!

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:52.720
Shut up! Would you just...

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:54.260
Bernie!

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:57.560
You're a good pilot, right? You can get him, right?!

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:08.070
Look. It's a bug.

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:10.820
We listened to everything you said...

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:12.780
...because we were afraid you'd tell someone about us.

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:14.740
All that stuff about being your friend was a lie.

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:21.540
Al, if you want to live, you have to run. Get off this colony.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.380
But what about everyone else?

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:31.590
Come on, we can still beat the Gundam. If we do that...

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:35.090
I'm running.

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:40.470
I HATE YOU!

00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:58.200
I'll tell the police.

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:00.200
If you do that, they'll execute you.

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:02.710
You're an accomplice, remember?!

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:30.320
All right!

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:50.960
Hey, kid. Why aren't you in school?

00:12:53.510 --> 00:12:56.970
<i>You're an accomplice.</i> <i>They'll execute you! Execute you!</i>

00:12:57.510 --> 00:12:58.470
Cutting class?

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:01.470
Hey, come back here!

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:41.970
Al?

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:48.100
What's wrong? Something bothering you?

00:13:48.190 --> 00:13:50.560
No, nothing.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:52.570
Anything I can do to help?

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:59.110
By the way, how's Bernie doing? I haven't seen him lately.

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:01.070
I don't know and I don't care!

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:05.740
Okay, what's wrong?

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:08.750
Okay, suppose... Just suppose that you knew...

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:13.040
...a space fleet was coming to destroy the colony.

00:14:13.130 --> 00:14:14.460
What would you do, Chris?

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:17.920
I think I'd fight.

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:20.590
You wouldn't run away?

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:23.220
No, I don't think I would.

00:14:23.260 --> 00:14:24.850
Wouldn't you be scared?

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:29.600
Of course I'd be scared. But I can handle being scared.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:32.020
What I couldn't handle was being left alone.

00:14:32.020 --> 00:14:33.900
Left alone?

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:37.860
If I lost my mom and dad and you and my friends...

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:42.160
If everyone who's special to me were killed and only I lived.

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:46.740
I couldn't live with myself if I ran away and left them all to die.

00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:49.830
So, only a coward runs away, right?

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:55.130
No, that's not what I mean. If I fight, it's for my own sake.

00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:58.710
I'd fight because I'd be scared of being left alone.

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:02.090
But that's what I'd do.

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.050
Another person may want to run.

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:09.060
Everyone has to decide for themselves which choice to make.

00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:12.520
If you fight, people may die...

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:15.690
But if you don't fight, people may still die.

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:19.070
There's no "right" or "wrong" choice to make.

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:21.740
All you can try is to do what you think is right.

00:15:23.990 --> 00:15:26.450
I think I answered you more than I should have. Sorry.

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:29.080
That's okay. Thanks!

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:32.250
Oh, say hi to Bernie for me if you see him!

00:15:54.020 --> 00:15:55.310
Is there a ship?

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:56.400
Where to?

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:57.440
Anywhere.

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.980
Oh, come on. Anywhere during a <i>war?</i>

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:14.790
Francheska will be fine. One, please.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:19.630
That'll be 520 hytes.

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:33.140
Hey! Keep outta here!

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:36.770
Lemme go! Where's Chay? Where's Telcott? Where's everyone?!

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:40.520
How should I know? Now go home!

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:44.280
Idiot! Jerk!

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:48.410
Hey! You're in here, too?!

00:16:49.660 --> 00:16:51.450
Cut it out!

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:56.620
Chay! Telcott! Hey!

00:16:57.460 --> 00:16:59.960
- Hey, it's Al.
- Yeah.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:03.170
You didn't come to school yesterday.

00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:08.640
It was cool! A Zeon mobile suit came and blew it up!

00:17:08.680 --> 00:17:12.060
- What about everyone?
- Everyone? What do you mean?

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:14.480
Was everyone in school all right?!

00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:16.770
Huh? Are you stupid?

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:19.610
That suit attacked during the night!

00:17:20.110 --> 00:17:21.110
Oh...

00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:22.820
What's wrong?

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:26.530
Well, you said "you didn't come to school," so I thought...

00:17:26.570 --> 00:17:28.240
We came.

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:30.320
Right after the attack.

00:17:32.240 --> 00:17:35.580
Hey, lemme show you something cool.

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:37.920
Ta-daa!

00:17:37.960 --> 00:17:39.080
Ta-daa!

00:17:39.170 --> 00:17:41.630
This is today's haul.

00:17:41.710 --> 00:17:44.710
The smell's still fresh. Wanna sniff it?

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:50.220
Don't look so sad. I'll give you some. Okay?

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:55.430
Al, what's wrong?

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:58.190
Don't cry! Cheer up!

00:17:58.230 --> 00:18:00.440
They're all over the place.

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:08.740
That's it, laugh! Right?

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:26.710
Captain, we have a message from Commander Killing.

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:28.380
Patch it through.

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:33.390
<i>The launch time</i> <i>has been determined.</i>

00:18:33.430 --> 00:18:36.680
<i>25 December,</i> <i>on the stroke of midnight.</i>

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:38.810
We're loading the missile now.

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:44.360
Killing... You're serious about using that thing?

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:47.070
<i>Are you objecting to</i> <i>headquarters' decision?</i>

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:48.490
No, sir...

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:51.910
<i>You were given this mission</i> <i>because of your abilities.</i>

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:53.950
<i>Am I making myself clear?</i>

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:54.700
Yes, sir.

00:18:54.740 --> 00:18:56.030
<i>Good luck to you.</i>

00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:03.750
So, how does this look?

00:19:05.130 --> 00:19:09.760
<i>I'll tell them everything.</i> <i>Then they'll understand.</i>

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:13.340
<i>I don't care if they execute me!</i> <i>I can't live all alone!</i>

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:18.770
What?! Oh, this is an emergency! You'd better escape, quick!

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:19.930
It's true!

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:21.980
Well, you'd better get out of here, then.

00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:24.520
A Zeon fleet's coming here on Christmas day!

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:28.320
Right, right. Very serious stuff. Very serious.

00:19:28.360 --> 00:19:29.820
You've gotta believe me!

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:32.780
I remember you! You're the kid who dragged us out...

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:35.700
...on that wild goose chase a few days ago!

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:37.740
I'm telling the truth this time!

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:39.830
Get outta here before I call your parents!

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:43.830
Everyone's gonna die, you idiot!

00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:50.420
You're gonna die! Then you'll be sorry!

00:19:50.670 --> 00:19:58.390
<i>Attention passengers on</i> <i>NTW flight 205 to Francheska.</i>

00:19:58.430 --> 00:20:02.020
<i>We will begin boarding</i> <i>in thirty minutes.</i>

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:12.190
Chris...

00:20:26.920 --> 00:20:28.670
Hello, sir.

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:31.380
Can I get you a drink?

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:34.510
Um, whiskey... With soda.

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:35.800
All right, sir.

00:20:35.840 --> 00:20:38.300
I'll have a whiskey over here, too.

00:20:38.350 --> 00:20:41.520
Miss, don't you think you've had enough?

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:46.520
What, he can drink, but I can't?

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:48.230
One whiskey.

00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:50.020
Make it a double.

00:20:54.070 --> 00:20:56.490
There you go. That'll be three hytes, five kules, please.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:06.920
Thank you, sir.

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:14.510
The money's on the counter.

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:25.600
Yeah, it's me. Just wanted to say I'm taking your advice...

00:21:25.640 --> 00:21:28.730
...and leaving for beautiful Francheska.

00:21:29.270 --> 00:21:32.230
You're probably glad I'm out of your hair.

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:34.820
Hope you enjoy your life with her.

00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:41.580
No, I'm not drunk! Yeah, I had a little to drink...

00:21:41.620 --> 00:21:45.330
...but I'm not drunk. I wish I was!

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:50.380
You were the one who said "let's get married!"

00:21:50.420 --> 00:21:52.500
It was all a lie!

00:21:57.970 --> 00:22:00.800
I don't want to go there!

00:22:01.930 --> 00:22:06.390
Francheska... Francheska's a horrible colony!

00:22:06.640 --> 00:22:11.610
<i>NTW flight 205, now boarding.</i>

00:22:11.650 --> 00:22:15.440
You're stringing her along with your lies, too.

00:22:15.440 --> 00:22:17.280
Just like you did with me!

00:22:17.320 --> 00:22:19.700
You don't even have the guts to keep on lying!

00:22:19.740 --> 00:22:20.780
That's a lie!

00:22:20.820 --> 00:22:22.530
Bernie, you're a good pilot, right?!

00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:25.160
Can you beat it, Bernie?

00:22:29.370 --> 00:22:31.710
I like this colony.

00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:34.420
Piece of cake?

00:22:52.900 --> 00:22:56.820
Before we eat, I have to tell you something about your father.

00:22:56.860 --> 00:22:58.490
You're getting a divorce?

00:22:58.530 --> 00:23:01.820
No, Daddy's coming home!

00:23:01.860 --> 00:23:02.660
When?

00:23:02.700 --> 00:23:04.490
Christmas.

00:23:04.530 --> 00:23:05.780
For how long?

00:23:05.830 --> 00:23:07.370
Forever.

00:23:07.870 --> 00:23:10.870
Daddy and I have made up.

00:23:11.710 --> 00:23:14.210
What's wrong? You aren't happy about it?

00:23:15.710 --> 00:23:18.880
All three of us will be together as a family from now on.

00:23:30.390 --> 00:23:34.600
<i>Dad's coming back.</i>
<i>Now he's gonna die.</i>

00:23:34.650 --> 00:23:36.690
<i>Everybody's gonna die!</i>

00:23:38.730 --> 00:23:39.690
Al?

00:23:42.360 --> 00:23:44.610
Telephone. Someone named Bernie.

00:23:59.250 --> 00:24:00.840
Hello? Hello?

00:24:01.630 --> 00:24:05.390
<i>Bernie? Bernie,</i> <i>is that you? Bernie!</i>

00:24:05.760 --> 00:24:07.680
Yeah, it's me.

00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:12.350
Bernie, look... I'm sorry about what I said before.

00:24:12.390 --> 00:24:16.350
Please, you've gotta help us. Bernie!

00:24:16.900 --> 00:24:19.440
Yeah. I think I will.

00:24:19.480 --> 00:24:20.570
Really?!

00:24:20.650 --> 00:24:26.240
Yeah. I've decided to try one more attack to get it.

00:24:26.280 --> 00:24:28.120
Will you help me?

00:24:28.160 --> 00:24:32.250
Yeah. Of course! Oh, thank you, Bernie!

00:24:32.290 --> 00:24:34.620
If we try it together, I just know we can do it!

00:24:34.870 --> 00:24:37.960
Yeah... Sure we will.

00:24:38.000 --> 00:24:40.670
<i>I love you, Bernie.</i>

00:24:40.750 --> 00:24:42.130
Stupid kid.

00:25:20.620 --> 00:25:26.400
<i>On that night I told them that lie...</i>

00:25:20.620 --> 00:25:26.400
<i>uso wo tsuita yoru ni wa</i>

00:25:26.990 --> 00:25:33.130
<i>...I couldn't sleep. That's how scared I was.</i>

00:25:26.990 --> 00:25:33.130
<i>nemurezu ni kowakatta</i>

00:25:33.460 --> 00:25:39.540
<i>But no matter how bad of a fight we would have...</i>

00:25:33.460 --> 00:25:39.540
<i>donna kenka wo shite mo</i>

00:25:39.840 --> 00:25:46.410
<i>...by the next day, it would be forgotten.</i>

00:25:39.840 --> 00:25:46.410
<i>tsugi no hi wa wasureteita</i>

00:25:48.710 --> 00:25:53.890
<i>The sky would be so blue...</i>

00:25:48.710 --> 00:25:53.890
<i>sora ga aoi koto</i>

00:25:55.150 --> 00:26:01.230
<i>...and that would make me so glad.</i>

00:25:55.150 --> 00:26:01.230
<i>sore ga ureshikute</i>

00:26:01.860 --> 00:26:07.740
<i>There would be times when I'd doubt others...</i>

00:26:01.860 --> 00:26:07.740
<i>itsuka hito wo utagai</i>

00:26:08.360 --> 00:26:14.680
<i>...and I'd know the loneliness of living.</i>

00:26:08.360 --> 00:26:14.680
<i>itsuka hito wo utagai</i>

00:26:14.740 --> 00:26:20.740
<i>But that was something I didn't notice then.</i>

00:26:14.740 --> 00:26:20.740
<i>ki ga tsukazu ni subete wo</i>

00:26:21.140 --> 00:26:26.180
<i>Back when I believed in everything...</i>

00:26:21.140 --> 00:26:26.180
<i>shinjiteta koro</i>

00:26:50.250 --> 00:26:52.250
NEXT EPISODE

00:26:53.110 --> 00:26:55.160
<i>Lieutenant Mackenzie, move out!</i>

00:26:56.200 --> 00:26:56.950
Roger!

00:26:57.490 --> 00:26:58.950
I don't have enough weapons.

00:26:59.530 --> 00:27:01.200
It's just like a treasure hunt!

00:27:02.290 --> 00:27:03.910
I'll fight it in the forest.

00:27:14.630 --> 00:27:16.340
Bernie!

00:27:16.570 --> 00:27:18.400
WAR IN THE POCKET

00:27:18.400 --> 00:27:20.280
Episode 6 War in the Pocket
